title: Presidential Elections
subtitle: It is time to elect a successor to Paul Doumer
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1932 and president = "Vacant"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
priority: -1000

= The President Election of 1932.

On May 10th, the Senate and the Chamber of Deputies convened to elect a new President after Paul Doumer's demise. His potential successor will have to gather a majority of the votes cast in order to win. 

Unfortunately for us, the new Chamber of Deputies did not have the time to convene, and it is thus the <span style="color: #C0A054;">right-</span><span style="color: #0087DC;">wing</span> dominated Chamber elected in 1928 that will take part in the election. Due to this and our weak presence in the Senate, it is certain that the next president will not be a <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span>. However, given the <span style="color: #c7017f;">Radical</span> strength in the upper house, a joint candidate of the Left might certainly win.

- @painleve
- @paulfaure

@painleve 
title: Propose Paul Painlevé's candidacy.
subtitle: A member of the <span style="color: #FF8000;">PRS</span>, Painlevé is acceptable to the whole left, but is he the preferred candidate of the <span style="color: #c7017f;">Radicals</span> ?
on-arrival: prrrs_relation -= 5; president = "Lebrun";

@paulfaure
title: Do not attempt a joint left-wing candidacy, and nominate Paul Faure instead.
subtitle: There is no hope for Painlevé, so we will nominate our General Secretary.
on-arrival: {!
Q.lebrun_votes = 0;
Q.faure_votes = 0;
Q.cachin_votes = 0;

Q.lebrun_votes += Q.na_z_r;
Q.lebrun_votes += Q.na_fr_r;
Q.lebrun_votes += Q.na_others_r;
Q.faure_votes += Q.na_sfio_r;
Q.cachin_votes += Q.na_pcf_r;

!}

Results:

<span style="color: #C0A054;">Albert Lebrun</span> - [+ lebrun_votes +]%

<span style="color: #c00000;">Paul Faure</span> - [+ faure_votes +]%

<span style="color: #700000;">Marcel Cachin</span> - [+ cachin_votes +]%

With [+ lebrun_votes +]%, Albert Lebrun has been elected President !
